---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { LAST_UPDATED, CLARITY_ID } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title="Cookies on MBA Worth: none, and how to check it in your browser" description="MBA Worth stores nothing on your device: the salary, school and scholarship you type stay in the open page. How to confirm it in your browser's developer tools in a minute." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Cookies' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none prose-headings:font-serif">
    <h1>Cookies</h1>
    <p>No cookie, no local storage. Your current salary, the school you pick and the scholarship you expect exist only in the page you have open, and disappear when you close it.</p>
    <h2>So no consent banner</h2>
    <p>Consent is required before a site writes non-essential information on your device. This site writes none. {CLARITY_ID ? 'The stability monitoring with Microsoft Clarity described in the privacy policy runs in a mode that stores nothing on your device.' : 'No analytics or advertising script is loaded.'}</p>
    <h2>Checking it yourself</h2>
    <p>Press F12 (or Option-Command-I on a Mac), open the Application or Storage tab and watch Cookies and Local Storage while you change the school or your salary in a calculator: both stay empty, and the Network tab records no request when the payback figure moves.</p>
    <p>See also the <a href={route('privacy', lang)}>privacy policy</a>. Updated: {LAST_UPDATED}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
